  "contract_review": {
    "role_authority": "One immutable ROOTS table owns qualification=build/software-qualification, delivery=build/delivery, job_identity=build/job-identities/software-qualification. Plan CLI derives the original identity selectors from its first2 roles and output from third. Packaging includes all3 exact trees rather than selected OCI files.",
    "inventory": "Hidden files, zero-byte files, empty directories, regular file bytes and portable-evidence permission bits0o777 are inventoried. Symlink/special paths, symlink ancestors and alias role-root inode pairs reject. Whole source membership/file hashes plus dev/inode/type-mode/size/uid/gid/mtime_ns/ctime_ns signatures are compared after streaming and after package validation; atime is ignored. No promise of preventing an external unobserved change after the call returns.",
    "outputs": "Fresh prepare and join destinations reject overlap with owned input trees. No move/delete/hardlink of original tree files is used. CLI control output checks protected-root/output overlap and existing nlink1 regular-file shape, so it cannot append to a hardlinked protected file. Dedicated concurrent hostile-mount proof is not claimed.",
    "stream_and_bounds": "Gzip TAR streams through SplitWriter directly into <=8 parts; production CLI uses fixed256MiB, MAX_BYTES8GiB, MAX_FILES100000, core64MiB. Internal tiny splitter sizes are test-only parameters, not CLI cap lowering. Exact multiples do not add an empty part. Ninth-part failure closes partial output without qualified success.",
    "part_join": "Only exact part-000..count-1 directory membership is accepted. Count1..8, true integer nonbool ordinals/offsets/sizes, contiguous offsets, full nonfinal256MiB size, per-file before/after identity, each SHA and complete joined archive size/SHA are checked; fresh output is never an overwrite.",
    "framing": "Full bounded single gzip decompression checks CRC/ISIZE, eof and rejects concatenated/trailing compressed data. TAR paths/count/types/duplicates are checked; logical parser seeks to archive.offset before requiring all-zero tail and at least2 end blocks, catching malformed or short first padding headers. Existing store.verify_package then checks complete manifest/modes/content, and store.restore_tree is exercised by tiny roundtrip.",
    "sparse_and_logical_bounds": "FinalR2 rejects any member.sparse value and any GNU.sparse PAX metadata before generic store extraction. Each member logical size and cumulative file payload size excluding the delivery manifest must be within8GiB. This closes the real R1 sparse/logical-admission defect without altering generic store.",
    "identity_closure": "Core identity record canonical selfhash/kind/schema/logical job, expected source commit, run and attempt, permitted original result, and clean source for original success are validated. The archived identity file SHA must equal exact original core identity bytes. Every qualification/delivery file path+size+SHA, including empty files and hidden names, must equal the complete original job artifact list; roots and duplicate refs reject. This is consistency of an unsigned source-bound record, not proof that a caller cannot fabricate a new complete record.",
    "uploads": "Eight explicit static pinned upload steps each carry exactly one part, with compression0/hidden/error-on-missing/30day retention and source/run/attempt/ordinal names. always() makes later uploads and core attempt despite a prior part failure. Finish requires every used slot success plus numeric unique artifact ID and64hex digest; unused slots must be absent/skipped. Partial finish returnsnonzero and records partial; core uploads last. Its own upload/final job/API admission remains external, explicitly never inferred.",
    "workflow_failure_path": "Prepare failure preserves original roots and uses the existing monolithic failure-only uploader; it can remain too large and unadmitted. No continue-on-error, matrix rebuild, custom network/container implementation or altered B=T identity appears. Original identity is captured before packing; its success cannot override a later upload or final-job failure."
  },
